I'd like to relativise that a bit; from the four Big Baddies Juiblex
is trivially to defeat with a wand of digging and a toothpick, while
Asmodeus, Baalzebub, and Orcus just leave the place before you kill
them. For the latter, if you occupy the upstairs, with a silver weapon
you can reduce the time to kill them (thus reducing the time where
some may, e.g., summon Demogorgon), but otherwise two-weaponing with
+6/+7 solves the problem as well quite fast. From the less important
demons; balrogs are slow, other hordes of deamons are mostly asleep.
Silver is somewhat interesting for the various ranks of vampires (but
an alternative is also e.g. Excalibur). The important liches are also
susceptible to silver, but for the major types the same holds that
has been said about the major demons; they teleport away. The most
interesting application of silver weapons are IMO the shades at Orcus'
town. (Did I forget any somewhat relevant silver hater?) Ah, yes;
nalfeshnees are very nasty because they summon nasties.
(But the problem with spellcasters is that they may neither come
in melee range nor in line of fire to perform their summoning.)

WRT "strongest and most important to take out quickly" I disagree.
Assuming I really want to always melee them, I'd put spellcasters
and tough and hard hitting monsters on that list, including golden
nagas, Olog-hai, dragons, minotaurs, and later the air elementals
on the planes. Very few of those that can't be avoided are silver
haters.

Other tough monster (that cannot be genocided as well) which are
not susceptible to silver are the various priests in the Sanctum.

That said, it's still not a bad decision to use a silver saber in
Gehennom.

